    "details": "<p><strong>AI/ML</strong> + <strong>WEB 3 / WEB 2</strong> + <strong>Blockchain </strong>+ <strong>Cybersec </strong>+ <strong>Open Source</strong>,etc | All Domains at one - Use cases of <strong>ETH</strong>, <strong>Solana</strong> contracts - <strong>Agentic AI </strong>pipeplines - Open Source models like <strong>Qwen</strong> <strong>Gemma</strong> - Scalable Innovations - <strong>CASCADE<br /></strong><br />CASCADE&nbsp; is the <strong>flagship hackathon</strong> of TantraFiesta 2026 at <strong>IIIT Nagpur</strong>, organised by <strong>CRISPR &times; ELEVATE</strong>. It is a <strong>24-hour </strong>offline hackathon&nbsp; with a <strong>prize pool of upto 2 lakhs</strong> including cash &amp; goodies, where teams build practical solutions to real-world problems across four themes.</p>\n<p><strong>Team Formation &amp; Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Team Size:</strong> 3&ndash;4 members. [Inter-college teams allowed]</li>\n<li><strong>Registration:</strong> Only the Team Leader needs to submit the team registration.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 1 Requirements:</strong> GitHub profile links of all members, along with relevant repositories, projects, or portfolio links.</li>\n<li><strong>Offline Shortlist:</strong> Top 60 teams from Round 1.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Online GitHub &amp; Portfolio Screening</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Dates:</strong> 14&ndash;21 October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Online</li>\n<li><strong>Format:</strong> GitHub profiles, repositories, previous projects, and portfolio screening</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Teams will be evaluated on their previous work, technical skills, individual contributions, and problem-solving ability. <br />The <strong>Team Leader</strong> must provide the required links and details for every team member. The top 60 teams will qualify for the offline hackathon.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 Evaluation Criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Project Quality &amp; Technical Depth:</strong> Quality, complexity, functionality, and relevance of previous projects.</li>\n<li><strong>Individual Contribution &amp; Collaboration:</strong> Evidence of each member&rsquo;s contribution and collaborative development.</li>\n<li><strong>Portfolio &amp; Problem-Solving Ability:</strong> Project documentation, practical thinking, and ability to build usable solutions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: CASCADE &mdash; 24-Hour Offline Hackathon</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Dates:</strong> 25&ndash;26 October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> 11:00 AM on 25 October to 11:00 AM on 26 October</li>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Offline</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> IIIT Nagpur Campus</li>\n<li><strong>Format:</strong> 24-hour hackathon across four real-world themes</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will develop practical solutions to real-world problems. The round will feature a Mid-Evaluation, peer engagement through the Stars system, and a separate Side Quest.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 Evaluation Criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Problem Understanding &amp; Relevance:</strong> How effectively the team addresses the chosen problem.</li>\n<li><strong>Innovation &amp; Creativity:</strong> Originality and usefulness of the solution.</li>\n<li><strong>Technical Implementation:</strong> Quality of implementation and demonstrable progress.</li>\n<li><strong>Feasibility &amp; Real-World Impact:</strong> Practicality and potential impact.</li>\n<li><strong>Execution &amp; Completeness:</strong> Quality and completeness of the solution within the given time.</li>\n<li><strong>Demo &amp; Presentation:</strong> Clarity of the demonstration and explanation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Mid-Evaluation</strong></p>\n<p>The Mid-Evaluation will take place at approximately <strong>11:00 PM on 25 October 2026</strong>. Mentors will assess the team's problem understanding, solution approach, technical progress, technologies used, feasibility, and implementation plan.</p>\n<p>Teams should be prepared to explain their progress and demonstrate the work completed so far.</p>\n<p><strong>Stars &mdash; Peer Engagement System</strong></p>\n<p>The Stars system allows teams to explore other projects and recognise promising ideas and execution.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team will receive Star stickers marked with its own team letter.</li>\n<li>Teams can award their Stars to other teams during designated engagement windows.</li>\n<li><strong>Self-voting is not allowed.</strong></li>\n<li>Stars will contribute a limited portion of the overall evaluation score.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The organisers will supervise and validate the Stars count.</p>\n<p><strong>Side Quest</strong></p>\n<p>The Side Quest is a separate challenge conducted alongside the main hackathon. It opens at <strong>12:00 AM on 26 October 2026</strong> and has its own winner recognition and evaluation.</p>\n<p>Further challenge instructions will be communicated by the organisers.</p>\n<p><strong>Multiple Themes &amp; Prize Stacking</strong></p>\n<p>Teams may participate in multiple themes and win awards in more than one theme. <strong>Prize stacking is allowed</strong>, including winning additional awards, provided the team meets the eligibility criteria for each award.</p>\n<p><strong>Best Women in Tech Team Award</strong></p>\n<p>This award recognises an outstanding team consisting <strong>entirely of women</strong>. It is separate from the main theme prizes, and eligible teams can receive it alongside other awards.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must have <strong>3&ndash;4 members</strong> and provide accurate registration details.</li>\n<li>All submitted work must be original or appropriately credited; plagiarism and misrepresentation are prohibited.</li>\n<li>Teams may compete in multiple themes and win multiple awards, subject to each award&rsquo;s eligibility criteria.</li>\n<li>Self-voting in the Stars system is not allowed.</li>\n<li>Participants must follow organiser instructions and maintain respectful conduct.</li>\n<li>Judges&rsquo; decisions will be final, subject to the officially published event rules.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>#CASCADE #INNOVATION #RAG #LANGCHAIN # NEURALNETWORKS</p>",
